// `pnpm tauri:mock`: `tauri dev` with this merged over tauri.conf.json.
// The real window -- its title bar, traffic lights, drag regions, size --
// around the browser preview's mock front end (docs/ui-preview.md), to
// look at the window without Canager looking at this Mac.
//
// Why nothing real runs:
//
// - The page is Vite in mock mode (`vite --mode mock`, as `pnpm dev:mock`
//   runs it) on a port of its own, 1440: not `pnpm dev`'s 1420, which
//   serves the real front end, and not the browser preview's 1430, so a
//   preview left open does not stand in for this one. In that mode
//   `@tauri-apps/api/core` is src/dev/mockTauri.ts, and src/lib/api.ts,
//   the one module that talks to the backend, talks to the mock: no
//   command reaches src-tauri/src/ipc.rs. Nor does the page badge the
//   Dock icon: `@tauri-apps/api/window` is src/dev/mockTauriWindow.ts. Nor
//   does the Unknown page's Show in Finder reach Finder:
//   `@tauri-apps/plugin-opener` is src/dev/mockTauriOpener.ts.
// - The Rust side starts nothing by itself. `run()` in
//   src-tauri/src/lib.rs builds `AppState` (it reads settings.json and
//   runs nothing) and spawns `ipc::refresh_on_background_change`, which
//   refreshes only when `Session::background_change` fires: when a
//   `brew update` that a refresh left running ends. Only the page starts
//   a refresh, and this page never reaches the backend, so no refresh
//   runs here, and no command. It puts up the menu bar too
//   (src-tauri/src/menu.rs), which runs nothing either: its items are
//   macOS's own -- Hide, Quit, Copy -- or bring the window back and tell
//   the page, which does not listen here (src/dev/mockTauriEvent.ts).
// - What runs at every launch runs here too: the login shell
//   `fix-path-env` asks for `PATH`, which runs no command
//   (docs/what-we-run.md, "How Canager runs anything").
// - Its own identifier, so its own folder: the mock window never reads
//   the app's settings.json, and keeps its size and position apart from
//   the app's.
//
// `beforeDevCommand` starts only the server the window loads, and `tauri
// dev` stops it as the app quits -- closing the window only hides it;
// `--strictPort` makes it fail rather than move to another port while the
// window loads whatever answers on 1440.
// Plain JSON apart from these comments (src/test/windowChrome.test.ts
// reads it so).
{
  "identifier": "com.brulek.canager.mock",
  "build": {
    "beforeDevCommand": "pnpm exec vite --mode mock --port 1440 --strictPort",
    "devUrl": "http://localhost:1440"
  }
}
